WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.080
- Welcome back, y'all.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.030
You might remember this story we featured

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:04.440
on the show last season.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:06.840
Students in an Atlanta
elementary school were asked

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.670
to dress as their favorite hero.

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.540
This is so cool.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.080
A young boy named Luke chose
his teacher, Mr. Freeman.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:17.160
Luke said his teacher
is a hero to every kid

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:18.660
because he's kind and thoughtful.

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:19.980
So let's look back.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.990
- I'm the only Black male
teacher at my school out

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.670
of 54 teachers.
- Wow.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:25.560
- So for him to see himself in me,

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.210
it really was special for me.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:30.330
- He's inspiring, kind,

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:35.070
funny, brave, and I thought
it'd make him happy.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:37.530
- Oh my gosh, that's so sweet.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.150
- Have over 20 years
of experience teaching,

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:41.250
and I was gonna leave
the field of education.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.960
I was gonna go into medical sales.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.290
I had already said that
year five, I'm leaving.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.490
But that wasn't my gift.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.475
My wife said to me, "Your gift is kids."

00:00:49.475 --> 00:00:50.930
(audience applauds)

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:52.710
- Here's where it gets really amazing.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:54.570
A grandmother in Virginia
watched that episode

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:57.390
and wondered if Mr. Freeman
could help her grandson.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:58.770
So she tracked him down

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.200
and what happened next
changed all of their lives.

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.720
It's an incredible story in
what we call Best In Class.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.280
(upbeat music)

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.109
♪ Best in class ♪

00:01:09.109 --> 00:01:12.300
- Please welcome back to
the show, Mr. Freeman,

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.751
along with Denita, the grandmother
who reached out to him.

00:01:15.751 --> 00:01:17.704
(audience cheers)

00:01:17.704 --> 00:01:19.238
So let's, welcome to the show,

00:01:19.238 --> 00:01:20.071
first of all.
- Thank you.

00:01:20.071 --> 00:01:20.904
Thank you very much.

00:01:20.904 --> 00:01:22.650
- What struck you about Mr. Freeman?

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.910
- Watching that episode and I saw,

00:01:26.910 --> 00:01:29.970
first I heard that Mr.
Freeman was the only

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.460
Black male teacher in the whole school.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:36.120
However, this young boy,
who happened to be white,

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.770
saw something in him that
compelled him to become the hero,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.260
for him to dress like him for that day.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.030
- Yeah.
- It just made me know

00:01:45.030 --> 00:01:48.060
that he can reach children
in a different way.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.590
That meant so much to me.

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.110
I had to reach out to Mr. Freeman.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.640
I had to find him

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:56.940
because I wanted to talk to
him about my own grandson.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.000
- Yeah. So what was Tre
like before Mr. Freeman?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.240
- So, Tre, Tre I think
is the best human being.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.740
I love him so much.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:09.000
But Tre is a very, he was
quiet, kind of withdrawn.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.430
Tre didn't do a lot, like with friends,

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.623
or he wasn't outgoing.
- Mm-hmm.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.550
- And he was in the fifth grade,

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:19.440
the last year of elementary school,

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.300
and he was about to go to middle school.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.890
And I was kind of concerned

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:25.620
because I wanted him to be able to fit in-

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.360
- And middle school is hard.
- In middle school.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.500
Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:31.290
- So that is why I reached out,

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.920
because I just wanted to, I
thought I was getting pointers,

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.230
some tips, you know, how to speak to him,

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:40.710
how to do things differently,
but not with Joe Freeman,

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:44.546
because Joe Freeman, he went all the way.

00:02:44.546 --> 00:02:48.540
He gave me the phone number
and this was on a Tuesday.

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:50.696
So your show was on a Monday.

00:02:50.696 --> 00:02:53.970
Because the very same day
that I watched the show,

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:55.500
I wrote the email.

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:58.170
And on that Tuesday, he reached out,

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:03.030
and he has been calling Tre
every Tuesday for a year, so.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:06.866
- Wow, the consistency.
(audience applauds)

00:03:06.866 --> 00:03:09.072
What have you noticed about Tre?

00:03:09.072 --> 00:03:10.950
Ever since working with him?
- Oh my God,

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:12.780
the changes in Tre are amazing.

00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.040
Tre has a lot of friends now.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.293
Tre, he used to.
(audience applauds)

00:03:20.293 --> 00:03:21.710
- So cute!
- Yeah.

00:03:23.843 --> 00:03:27.420
So that is actually a picture of,

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:29.280
Mr. Freeman went to Mexico

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.370
and he had on this cool outfit.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.377
- Mr. Freeman probably had a good time.

00:03:34.377 --> 00:03:38.640
- And Tre loved Mr.
Freeman's outfit in Mexico.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.650
And next thing I know, Tre got the outfit.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:41.900
- Aw, oh, that's so nice.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.783
- Yeah, so.
- You've given him confidence.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.040
- Yeah.
- Self confidence.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:52.830
- So Tre had, at the
end of the school year,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:56.730
elementary school, entered a rap battle,

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.350
which I would've never thought

00:03:58.350 --> 00:03:59.294
he would do.
- Yeah, you thought

00:03:59.294 --> 00:04:00.480
he'd been too shy.
- Yeah, he entered

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.335
the rap battle and won third place.

00:04:03.335 --> 00:04:05.841
- Wow.
(audience applauds)

00:04:05.841 --> 00:04:06.822
He had a lot to say.

00:04:06.822 --> 00:04:07.655
- He did.
- He was just keeping it

00:04:07.655 --> 00:04:09.150
to himself.
- And he couldn't wait

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:10.800
to share his information.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.130
Everything he does, he can't
wait to tell Mr. Freeman.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.613
So it is amazing.
- Man, that's so cool.

00:04:16.613 --> 00:04:18.150
- And and this is our first time.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:19.110
This is our first time meeting.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:21.302
- I've never met him before.
- I've never met her.

00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:22.135
I've never met her, yeah.

00:04:22.135 --> 00:04:24.090
- Everything has been over the phone.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.616
So I'm so super excited.

00:04:26.616 --> 00:04:29.460
I've never met him before
and Tre has never met him.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.170
- Yeah. Tre's never met.
- That's what I wanted say.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.420
So here's the deal, Tre has never met him,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:35.018
and they've been talking for a year.

00:04:35.018 --> 00:04:36.240
- Almost a year.
- By the way,

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:37.560
the consistency, man,

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.480
that's the coolest thing
that you can provide a kid.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:41.035
So thank you for that.
- Yeah.

00:04:41.035 --> 00:04:43.813
- Consistency is so amazing.
(audience applauds)

00:04:43.813 --> 00:04:47.850
But Tre thinks that he's here
to talk about his schoolwork.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:49.740
He has no idea Mr. Freeman is here.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.960
So we're going to have Mr. Freeman hide.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.130
You don't wanna miss the surprise.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.390
I don't either, stay right here.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.577
Tre is here today. Give it up a Tre.

00:04:56.577 --> 00:04:59.580
(audience cheers)

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:00.530
Look at that smile.

00:05:01.512 --> 00:05:03.780
- So Tre, how do you think Mr. Freeman

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.010
has kind of impacted your life?

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.390
How has he affected you?

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:09.570
- I'm lucky that Mr. Freeman as my mentor.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:12.360
- Yeah.
- He calls me every Tuesday.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:14.160
- [Kelly] Yeah, you look forward to that?

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.350
- Yes.
- Yeah. Absolutely.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.570
So I heard that you had your
first dance this weekend.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.100
Is that true?

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.990
- Yes.
- Do you like dancing?

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.850
I love dancing.

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:26.100
I mean, I will just dance
just right here for you.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.840
I love dancing.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.490
- Well it depends what song they play.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:31.980
- Exactly. It's gotta be a good DJ.

00:05:31.980 --> 00:05:34.050
We have an amazing DJ here,
Reuben. I'm just saying.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.886
He plays amazing music. So.

00:05:35.886 --> 00:05:37.305
(audience applauds)
I agree.

00:05:37.305 --> 00:05:38.527
It does depend on the song,

00:05:38.527 --> 00:05:40.710
but we love teachers on this show.

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:43.290
My mama was a teacher, so I
always try and lift up teachers

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.880
and just recognize how angelic they are.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:48.180
So what do you wanna say to Mr. Freeman?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.330
- He changed our lives and
thank you for everything.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.714
- Aw.
(audience applauds)

00:05:53.714 --> 00:05:56.464
Those are powerful words.

00:05:57.659 --> 00:05:58.830
Well, I have some good news,

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.000
'cause you can tell him that yourself.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.804
He's actually here. Come
on out, Mr. Freeman!

00:06:02.804 --> 00:06:05.637
(audience cheers)

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:10.522
- What's up big way Tre, what's up?

00:06:10.522 --> 00:06:12.621
How you doing?
- I'm good!

00:06:12.621 --> 00:06:16.025
- Oh my God!
- Give me a hug, yeah?

00:06:16.025 --> 00:06:18.608
You thought that I was shorter?

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:23.092
- Y'all wanna scoot and
then we'll sit, yeah?

00:06:23.092 --> 00:06:25.313
- There you go, just sit here.

00:06:25.313 --> 00:06:26.806
- Oh my gosh.

00:06:26.806 --> 00:06:28.121
What do you wanna say to Tre?

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:29.400
First of all, this is a big thing to like,

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.290
speak on a show like this,
man, you're doing well.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.220
- First of all, I'm proud of you.

00:06:32.220 --> 00:06:35.370
I'm proud of you for coming
to a new city, another state,

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.410
for even taking a chance to talk to me.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.574
The first thing he said to me,

00:06:38.574 --> 00:06:41.949
"I thought you were shorter." (laughs)

00:06:41.949 --> 00:06:43.367
So over the phone,

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:46.830
we've never had FaceTime anything,
so he just sees pictures,

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:48.600
so I guess, yeah.
- Oh wow.

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.250
- You look a lot taller right now.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:52.740
You look a lot taller.
- That's amazing.

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:54.240
- I'm just proud of you,
man. I'm proud of you.

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.950
I'm proud of the things you've been doing.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:57.600
I'm proud of the things you've done.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:59.610
- How does this
relationship make you feel?

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:01.440
This is amazing, this is
all from you being affected,

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:03.532
watching something, then
you actually acted on it,

00:07:03.532 --> 00:07:05.280
by the way.
- I did act on it,

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:08.269
and I got so much more
than I ever expected.

00:07:08.269 --> 00:07:10.420
I'm just overwhelmed because

00:07:11.576 --> 00:07:14.310
(audience applauds)

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:17.292
not only is he there for Tre,

00:07:17.292 --> 00:07:20.100
he's become family.

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.070
And we talk about everything, we talk,

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:24.630
as well as them talking.

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:27.240
So we talk about everything I know,

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:30.030
about graduations or going to college,

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:32.490
buying a new house, eating crabs.

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:35.070
I mean, we talk about everything.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:39.720
So it really is a family,
I think, on both sides, so.

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:41.670
- I think it's so good too to have people

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.650
outside your family to
have those relationships

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.230
with as well, because you might
open up in a different way.

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.300
So I think this is so special. So cool.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.133
- Yes, I do too.

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:50.490
And I just want to thank Mr. Denita.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.290
You know, Miss Denita,
I just want you to know

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:54.780
that I appreciate you
and I'm forever grateful

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.370
to be a part of your family.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.080
And the loving on him

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.300
allowed me to love on him
too, and I thank you for that.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:01.674
- Wow. Thank you.

00:08:01.674 --> 00:08:03.720
(audience applauds)

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:08.400
- Well, before we go, we
wanted to ask about Luke,

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.770
Mr. Freeman's student who was here before,

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.557
also known as Sir Luke.

00:08:12.557 --> 00:08:13.740
How's Luke doing,

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:14.850
- [Joe] Sir Luke's doing amazing.

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.560
Sir Luke, that's my guy.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:19.260
He comes, so Luke, that's him,

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:20.790
me giving him the book for the first time.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.170
- Yeah.
- His first time seeing it.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:23.190
I mentioned it on the show

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.990
that he was gonna be a
character in the book.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.347
Sir Luke's in the book,
he has on the same suit

00:08:27.347 --> 00:08:30.111
that he had on, that we
were on the show with.

00:08:30.111 --> 00:08:31.350
He's signing autographs.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:34.526
Anytime he's in my classroom,
he's signing autographs,

00:08:34.526 --> 00:08:36.780
he's high fiving kids in the hall.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:39.120
He's in fourth grade now.
So Luke's doing great.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:40.620
He's another example of confidence,

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.410
how believing in a child can really-

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:44.750
- Change the trajectory.
- Yes.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.788
- Absolutely.
- Absolutely.

00:08:46.788 --> 00:08:47.904
(audience applauds)

00:08:47.904 --> 00:08:51.150
Well, I love this whole story,
but I'm hardly the only one.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.610
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.290
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.930
want to celebrate the
powerful connection between

00:08:57.930 --> 00:08:59.250
Denita, Mr. Freeman, and Tre.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.130
So they're giving Tre $5,000.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:04.873
- Whoa!
(audience cheers)

00:09:10.823 --> 00:09:12.853
- That sound all right?
- Wow, thank you. Thank you.

00:09:12.853 --> 00:09:15.257
- Yes!
- Wow, thank you.

00:09:15.257 --> 00:09:16.745
Thank you.
- Oh my God.

00:09:16.745 --> 00:09:18.433
Have some fun. Do something fun with that.

00:09:18.433 --> 00:09:19.710
- Wow.
- Well, thank y'all

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:20.910
for coming on this show.
- How do you feel?

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.997
- How does that feel?
- I can go to college.

00:09:22.997 --> 00:09:26.836
- Oh my God.
(audience applauds)

00:09:26.836 --> 00:09:30.020
I love you so much that
that's where your brain went.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:33.030
If you ever need any extra
help on that, you let me know.

00:09:33.030 --> 00:09:34.590
I will always help with education.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:36.870
Oh my gosh. We need a
short break everybody.

